 of activation or correct agent behavior. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/trust-model#lifecycle-boundaries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle boundaries"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hook-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook support"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project scope"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User scope"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hooks installed"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".claude/settings.json"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"~/.claude/settings.json"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SessionStart"},{"type":"text","value":" skill catalog plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreToolUse"},{"type":"text","value":" edit gate"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".codex/hooks.json"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"~/.codex/hooks.json"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SessionStart"},{"type":"text","value":" skill catalog plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreToolUse"},{"type":"text","value":" edit gate; Codex hook interception is not a complete security boundary"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub Copilot CLI"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guidance via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".github/copilot-instructions.md"},{"type":"text","value":"; blocking hooks are not project-scoped"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$COPILOT_HOME/hooks/hooks.json"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"~/.copilot/hooks/hooks.json"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SessionStart"},{"type":"text","value":" skill catalog plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreToolUse"},{"type":"text","value":" edit gate in user scope"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cursor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guidance only"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guidance only"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" or Cursor rules; no blocking hook is installed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" agents"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guidance only"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guidance only"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent-skills"},{"type":"text","value":" guidance block; no blocking hook is installed"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".github/copilot-instructions.md"},{"type":"text","value":" is a supported project guidance target for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent install"},{"type":"text","value":". GitHub Copilot CLI hook enforcement uses the user-scoped Copilot hooks directory because that is the supported hook location."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codex requires users to review and trust non-managed hooks before they run. If Codex reports hooks awaiting review, open its hook browser and trust the generated Intent hook."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"status-messages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Status messages"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook installed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Installed Intent hooks for claude (project) in .claude/settings.json."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook skipped: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Skipped Intent hooks for copilot: project scope is not supported; use --scope user"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent install"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-list","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent list"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-load","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent load"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"behavior","text":"Behavior","level":2},{"id":"session-behavior","text":"Session behavior","level":3},{"id":"installation-behavior","text":"Installation behavior","level":3},{"id":"hook-support","text":"Hook support","level":2},{"id":"status-messages","text":"Status messages","level":2},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`intent hooks install` installs lifecycle hooks that surface available Intent skills and gate supported edit tools until they observe an Intent guidance check.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest hooks install [--scope project|user] [--agents copilot,claude,codex|all]\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Options\n\n- `--scope <scope>`: hook install scope, either `project` or `user`; defaults to `project`\n- `--agents <agents>`: comma-separated hook agents to configure (`copilot`, `claude`, `codex`) or `all`; defaults to `all`\n\n## Behavior\n\n### Session behavior\n\n- Installs hook behavior without writing an `intent-skills` guidance block.\n- Returns a session-start skill catalog as agent context with available `skill-id: description` entries.\n- Builds that catalog with the project's installed `@tanstack/intent` CLI when one is resolvable from `node_modules`. When that same installation has a `node_modules/.bin/intent` shim, the catalog suggests `node_modules/.bin/intent load <skill-id>` for loads; without a shim, or without a local install, it suggests the package-manager runner generated by Intent. Without a local install the catalog itself is also built through that runner.\n- Blocks supported edit tools until the hook observes a recognized `intent list` or `intent load <skill-id>` command, including the `node_modules/.bin/intent` form. If no listed skill matches the task, the agent can continue without loading one.\n- Uses `package.json#intent.skills` and `package.json#intent.exclude` to control which skills appear in the session catalog.\n\n### Installation behavior\n\n- `--scope project` writes project-local hook config for agents that support it.\n- `--scope user` writes user-level agent config and stores runner scripts under `~/.tanstack/intent/hooks`.\n- `--agents all` is the default. In project scope, Copilot is skipped because the supported Copilot CLI hook location is user-scoped.\n- Run `intent install` separately when you also want to write project guidance.\n\nThe hook records a recognized list or load command before that command completes.\n\nHooks do not verify that:\n\n- The command succeeded.\n- The selected skill matched the task.\n- The agent received the returned content.\n- The model applied the guidance.\n\nHook output is an edit gate and observation signal, not proof of activation or correct agent behavior. See [Lifecycle boundaries](../concepts/trust-model#lifecycle-boundaries).\n\n## Hook support\n\n| Agent | Project scope | User scope | Hooks installed |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Claude Code | `.claude/settings.json` | `~/.claude/settings.json` | `SessionStart` skill catalog plus `PreToolUse` edit gate |\n| Codex | `.codex/hooks.json` | `~/.codex/hooks.json` | `SessionStart` skill catalog plus `PreToolUse` edit gate; Codex hook interception is not a complete security boundary |\n| GitHub Copilot CLI | Guidance via `.github/copilot-instructions.md`; blocking hooks are not project-scoped | `$COPILOT_HOME/hooks/hooks.json` or `~/.copilot/hooks/hooks.json` | `SessionStart` skill catalog plus `PreToolUse` edit gate in user scope |\n| Cursor | Guidance only | Guidance only | Use `AGENTS.md` or Cursor rules; no blocking hook is installed |\n| Generic `AGENTS.md` agents | Guidance only | Guidance only | Use the `intent-skills` guidance block; no blocking hook is installed |\n\n`.github/copilot-instructions.md` is a supported project guidance target for `intent install`. GitHub Copilot CLI hook enforcement uses the user-scoped Copilot hooks directory because that is the supported hook location.\n\nCodex requires users to review and trust non-managed hooks before they run. If Codex reports hooks awaiting review, open its hook browser and trust the generated Intent hook.\n\n## Status messages\n\n- Hook installed: `Installed Intent hooks for claude (project) in .claude/settings.json.`\n- Hook skipped: `Skipped Intent hooks for copilot: project scope is not supported; use --scope user`\n\n## Related\n\n- [intent install](./intent-install)\n- [intent list](./intent-list)\n- [intent load](./intent-load)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: intent hooks\nid: intent-hooks\n---\n\n`intent hooks install` installs lifecycle hooks that surface available Intent skills and gate supported edit tools until they observe an Intent guidance check.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest hooks install [--scope project|user] [--agents copilot,claude,codex|all]\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Options\n\n- `--scope <scope>`: hook install scope, either `project` or `user`; defaults to `project`\n- `--agents <agents>`: comma-separated hook agents to configure (`copilot`, `claude`, `codex`) or `all`; defaults to `all`\n\n## Behavior\n\n### Session behavior\n\n- Installs hook behavior without writing an `intent-skills` guidance block.\n- Returns a session-start skill catalog as agent context with available `skill-id: description` entries.\n- Builds that catalog with the project's installed `@tanstack/intent` CLI when one is resolvable from `node_modules`. When that same installation has a `node_modules/.bin/intent` shim, the catalog suggests `node_modules/.bin/intent load <skill-id>` for loads; without a shim, or without a local install, it suggests the package-manager runner generated by Intent. Without a local install the catalog itself is also built through that runner.\n- Blocks supported edit tools until the hook observes a recognized `intent list` or `intent load <skill-id>` command, including the `node_modules/.bin/intent` form. If no listed skill matches the task, the agent can continue without loading one.\n- Uses `package.json#intent.skills` and `package.json#intent.exclude` to control which skills appear in the session catalog.\n\n### Installation behavior\n\n- `--scope project` writes project-local hook config for agents that support it.\n- `--scope user` writes user-level agent config and stores runner scripts under `~/.tanstack/intent/hooks`.\n- `--agents all` is the default. In project scope, Copilot is skipped because the supported Copilot CLI hook location is user-scoped.\n- Run `intent install` separately when you also want to write project guidance.\n\nThe hook records a recognized list or load command before that command completes.\n\nHooks do not verify that:\n\n- The command succeeded.\n- The selected skill matched the task.\n- The agent received the returned content.\n- The model applied the guidance.\n\nHook output is an edit gate and observation signal, not proof of activation or correct agent behavior. See [Lifecycle boundaries](../concepts/trust-model#lifecycle-boundaries).\n\n## Hook support\n\n| Agent | Project scope | User scope | Hooks installed |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Claude Code | `.claude/settings.json` | `~/.claude/settings.json` | `SessionStart` skill catalog plus `PreToolUse` edit gate |\n| Codex | `.codex/hooks.json` | `~/.codex/hooks.json` | `SessionStart` skill catalog plus `PreToolUse` edit gate; Codex hook interception is not a complete security boundary |\n| GitHub Copilot CLI | Guidance via `.github/copilot-instructions.md`; blocking hooks are not project-scoped | `$COPILOT_HOME/hooks/hooks.json` or `~/.copilot/hooks/hooks.json` | `SessionStart` skill catalog plus `PreToolUse` edit gate in user scope |\n| Cursor | Guidance only | Guidance only | Use `AGENTS.md` or Cursor rules; no blocking hook is installed |\n| Generic `AGENTS.md` agents | Guidance only | Guidance only | Use the `intent-skills` guidance block; no blocking hook is installed |\n\n`.github/copilot-instructions.md` is a supported project guidance target for `intent install`. GitHub Copilot CLI hook enforcement uses the user-scoped Copilot hooks directory because that is the supported hook location.\n\nCodex requires users to review and trust non-managed hooks before they run. If Codex reports hooks awaiting review, open its hook browser and trust the generated Intent hook.\n\n## Status messages\n\n- Hook installed: `Installed Intent hooks for claude (project) in .claude/settings.json.`\n- Hook skipped: `Skipped Intent hooks for copilot: project scope is not supported; use --scope user`\n\n## Related\n\n- [intent install](./intent-install)\n- [intent list](./intent-list)\n- [intent load](./intent-load)\n"}
